            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              Yes. According to the U.S. Fire Administration, dryers cause over 15,000 house fires annually, resulting in $35+ million in property damage. The leading cause is failure to clean vents. Lint is highly flammable, and when combined with the heat from your dryer and restricted airflow, it creates a serious fire hazard. Regular cleaning eliminates this risk.
            </p>
